# Allowlist for scripts/pclaude-check.sh. It lists text the check would flag
# in skills/pclaude/ but that is meant to be there.
#
# One entry per line:
#   <path glob, relative to skills/pclaude/><TAB><exact text on the flagged line>
# A hit is allowed only when the text it matched lies inside an occurrence of
# that exact text, on a line of a file the glob matches. `*` matches within a
# path segment and `**/` matches any number of directories.
#
# Every entry must sit in a block that opens with a `#` comment saying why it
# is allowed. A blank line ends a block. An entry without a comment fails the
# check, and an entry that no longer matches anything is printed as a warning
# so it can be deleted.

# The footer spec section 4 puts on every SKILL.md credits upstream by name.
# The two agents and CONVENTIONS.md (which states the footer) carry it too.
**/SKILL.md	Ported from pstack by poteto (MIT). See skills/pclaude/LICENSE.
agents/*.md	Ported from pstack by poteto (MIT). See skills/pclaude/LICENSE.
CONVENTIONS.md	`Ported from pstack by poteto (MIT). See skills/pclaude/LICENSE.`

# A template line in why's synthesizer prompt: `url` is a placeholder for the
# PR link the synthesizer fills in, not a relative file.
pclaude-why/references/synthesizer-prompt.md	[PR #123](url)

# CONVENTIONS.md holds the one substitutes table: it has to name each Cursor
# feature it replaces, so its heading, intro and rows are allowed.
CONVENTIONS.md	## Substitutes for Cursor features
CONVENTIONS.md	Upstream pstack was written for Cursor. Where it named a Cursor feature, pclaude uses the substitute below. A feature with no substitute is cut, along with every mention of it.
CONVENTIONS.md	| `deslop` (cursor-team-kit) | `pclaude-unslop` for prose, `/simplify` for code |
CONVENTIONS.md	| `control-ui` | the `claude-in-chrome` skill |
CONVENTIONS.md	| `control-cli` | the `run` skill, or tmux |
CONVENTIONS.md	| `AskQuestion` | numbered free-text questions, each with a recommendation (above) |
CONVENTIONS.md	| `Task` tool, background tasks | the Agent tool with `run_in_background: true` |
CONVENTIONS.md	| model slugs, `pstack-models.mdc`, `/setup-pstack` | a role in `models.md` |
CONVENTIONS.md	| `~/.cursor` transcripts | `~/.claude/projects`, read through the pclaude scripts package |
CONVENTIONS.md	| Custom Modes, `mode: true` | the user-invoked `/pclaude-poteto-mode <task>` |
